      "summary": "Kingdom of Argos / Hyborian Powers. A suave, exceptionally wealthy diplomat residing in Kordava's maritime district overlooking the Black River mouth. He offers trade alliances, naval escort agreements, and substantial foreign loans to the cash-strapped Triumvirate.",
      "atAGlance": {
        "appearance": "A plump, impeccably groomed diplomat dressed in layered purple and sea-green Argossean silk tunics, dripping with pearls and gold rings. A fine scented pomander ball hangs from his wrist.",
        "mannerisms": "Smooths his oiled beard with ringed fingers; laughs heartedly at his own court jokes while keen eyes assess room reactions.",
        "quote": "Argos desires only peace and open trade, my royal friends. Of course, peace requires a well-funded navy, and trade requires... concessions along the Baracha Strait.",
        "courtDCs": "DC 16 Insight to pierce his polite diplomatic overtures; DC 18 Persuasion/Negotiation to secure foreign loans without surrendering maritime sovereignty.",
        "publicStance": "A suave, exceptionally wealthy diplomat residing in Kordava's maritime district overlooking the Black River mouth. He offers trade alliances, naval escort agreements, and substantial foreign loans to the cash-strapped Triumvirate.",
        "secretAgenda": "Representing the merchant lords of Messantia (Argos), Tiberio seeks to exploit Zingara's political instability, gather intelligence on royal military weaknesses, fund privateer raids in the Baracha Strait to disrupt Zingaran maritime trade, and retrieve lost foreign diplomatic signets and relics buried during Period V.",
        "rival": "Vesper the Key-Master"
      },
      "content": "\n<div class=\"npc-header-card\">\n  <div class=\"npc-meta\">\n    <span class=\"badge faction-badge\">Kingdom of Argos / Hyborian Powers</span>\n    <span class=\"badge rival-badge\">Primary Rival: Vesper the Key-Master</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"at-a-glance-grid\">\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Visual Appearance:</strong> A plump, impeccably groomed diplomat dressed in layered purple and sea-green Argossean silk tunics, dripping with pearls and gold rings. A fine scented pomander ball hangs from his wrist.</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Mannerisms:</strong> Smooths his oiled beard with ringed fingers; laughs heartedly at his own court jokes while keen eyes assess room reactions.</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item quote\"><strong>Iconic Quote:</strong> &ldquo;Argos desires only peace and open trade, my royal friends. Of course, peace requires a well-funded navy, and trade requires... concessions along the Baracha Strait.&rdquo;</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item dcs\"><strong>Court Social DCs:</strong> DC 16 Insight to pierce his polite diplomatic overtures; DC 18 Persuasion/Negotiation to secure foreign loans without surrendering maritime sovereignty.</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Public Persona</h3>\n<p>A suave, exceptionally wealthy diplomat residing in Kordava's maritime district overlooking the Black River mouth. He offers trade alliances, naval escort agreements, and substantial foreign loans to the cash-strapped Triumvirate.</p>\n\n<div class=\"gm-callout\">\n  <div class=\"gm-badge\">GM CONFIDENTIAL &bull; SECRET AGENDA &amp; HIDDEN LEVER</div>\n  <p>Representing the merchant lords of Messantia (Argos), Tiberio seeks to exploit Zingara's political instability, gather intelligence on royal military weaknesses, fund privateer raids in the Baracha Strait to disrupt Zingaran maritime trade, and retrieve lost foreign diplomatic signets and relics buried during Period V.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Faction Ties &amp; Court Relationships</h3>\n<p>Maintains secret connections with rival grandees in the Eastern League. He exerts economic pressure directly on the Triumvirate, using foreign debt as a weapon to force diplomatic concessions.</p>\n\n<h3>Player-Led Plot Hooks</h3>\n\n<div class=\"hook-card info-card\">\n  <h4>Hook 1: Blood in the Cauldron</h4>\n  <p><strong>Premise:</strong>  Tiberio delivers an ultimatum: return the signet ring and remains of an Argossean ambassador murdered during King Daedalus's Period V ritual, or face an immediate naval blockade of Kordava harbor by the Argossean fleet.</p>\n<p><strong>Core Conflict & Player Choice:</strong>  The PCs must secretly enter an earthquake-exposed crypt beneath Kordava. Inside, they find the dead ambassador is now a conscious, memory-retaining zombie thrall guarding the Obsidian Blade. The PCs must choose to destroy the thrall for the signet ring, attempt a dangerous unbinding rite, or claim the Obsidian Blade for themselves.</p>\n<div class=\"dc-box\"><strong>Key Skill Checks: DC 15 History/Arcana (recognize unbinding ritual runes); DC 17 Persuasion (appeal to a thrall's living memories).</strong></div>\n<p class=\"escalation\"><strong>Dynamic Escalation Trigger: If the PCs take longer than 3 combat rounds negotiating inside the crypt, a covert strike team loyal to the Restoration Council enters from the upper shafts to seize the relic and kill all witnesses.</strong></p>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"hook-card info-card\">\n  <h4>Hook 2: The Barachan Maritime Deal</h4>\n  <p><strong>Premise:</strong>  Tiberio offers to pay off the royal household's immediate state debt if the Triumvirate signs a treaty granting Argossean warships free passage through the Baracha Strait to hunt \"Barachan pirates.\"</p>\n<p><strong>Core Conflict & Player Choice:</strong>  Accepting the deal solves the crown's immediate bankruptcy but surrenders Zingaran maritime sovereignty to their primary naval rival. Rejecting it causes immediate financial collapse.</p>\n<div class=\"dc-box\"><strong>Key Skill Checks: DC 16 History/Persuasion (re-negotiate treaty terms); DC 15 Insight (uncover secret privateer funding clauses).</strong></div>\n<p class=\"escalation\"><strong>Dynamic Escalation Trigger: Local Barachan pirate captains learn of the treaty negotiations and launch a daring night raid against the foreign embassy in Kordava, threatening to drag the kingdom into war.</strong></p>\n\n</div>\n\n",
      "gmSecrets": "Representing the merchant lords of Messantia (Argos), Tiberio seeks to exploit Zingara's political instability, gather intelligence on royal military weaknesses, fund privateer raids in the Baracha Strait to disrupt Zingaran maritime trade, and retrieve lost foreign diplomatic signets and relics buried during Period V.",
