      "summary": "Republican insurgents operating out of The Pit contact the PCs in secret during a royal diplomatic gala. They possess hard evidence proving ...",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Involved Factions:</strong> The Triumvirate, Republican Insurgents, Restoration Council, Church of Nemeth</p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic Reward:</strong> Secures absolute blackmail evidence against General Don Rodrigo and Marquis Mateo, allowing the PCs to purge their puppetmasters or force total political submission.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Narrative Premise</h3>\n<p>Republican insurgents operating out of The Pit contact the PCs in secret during a royal diplomatic gala. They possess hard evidence proving that the military chief and chief monarchist—the PCs' own puppetmasters—assassinated the republican founder during Period VI and framed the Church of Nemeth.</p>\n\n<h3>Core Conflict &amp; Player Choice</h3>\n<p>The republicans offer the evidence in exchange for royal pardons and democratic concessions. However, agents of the underground Church of Nemeth intercept the meeting, demanding the evidence to clear their church's name. The PCs must decide whether to use the evidence to blackmail their handlers, hand it to the church, or side with the Council.</p>\n\n<div class=\"dc-box\">\n  <strong>Suggested Skill Checks:</strong> DC 16 Stealth/Deception Check (slip away from royal handlers at gala); DC 14 Insight Check (detect double-dealing in church zealots).\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"escalation\"><strong>Dynamic Escalation Trigger:</strong> If the PCs hesitate or attempt to play all sides, the military chief's royal assassins strike the meeting place, attempting to burn the documents and silence all informants.</p>\n",
