      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Involved Factions:</strong> The Triumvirate, Restoration Council, Grandee Coalitions, Master Alchemist Vane</p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic Reward:</strong> Restores iron production to the royal armory while gaining a secret map to the subterranean crypt housing the Black Blade of Azur.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Narrative Premise</h3>\n<p>A crown-owned industrial zombie pit near Jerida collapses into an ancient river cavern, releasing hundreds of memory-retaining thralls who seize a vital iron mine. The Restoration Council uses the lost revenue as an excuse to cut the royal household's stipend, tightening their financial leash on the Triumvirate.</p>\n\n<h3>Core Conflict &amp; Player Choice</h3>\n<p>Traveling to Jerida under the guise of an inspection, the PCs discover the thralls are led by a reanimated Period IV scholar who offers to reveal a secret passage into the crypt of the Black Blade of Azur—an anti-sorcery weapon capable of severing Council magical control—if the rulers help the thralls escape to the Pictish Wilderness.</p>\n\n<div class=\"dc-box\">\n  <strong>Suggested Skill Checks:</strong> DC 14 Athletics/Survival Check (navigate toxic pit slurry); DC 16 Warfare/Tactics Check (organize stealth escape route through mountain passes).\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"escalation\"><strong>Dynamic Escalation Trigger:</strong> Reeking toxic alchemical fumes require a DC 13 Fortitude Save every 10 minutes; failure inflicts cumulative physical weakness (-1 to physical checks and attack rolls).</p>\n",
