      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Involved Factions:</strong> The Triumvirate, Restoration Council, Church of Nemeth, Kingdom of Argos</p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic Reward:</strong> Acquires waters from the Fountain of Youth in the Rabirian Mountains, providing an absolute cure for magical wasting poisons, disease, or necromantic decay affecting royal allies.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Narrative Premise</h3>\n<p>One of the PCs (or their sole loyal blood relative at court) is struck by a slow, magical wasting poison—secretly administered by the Restoration Council to remind the Triumvirate how easily they can be replaced. To survive without begging handlers for an antidote, the PCs must quietly ride into the Rabirian Mountains to locate the lost Fountain of Youth.</p>\n\n<h3>Core Conflict &amp; Player Choice</h3>\n<p>The PCs locate the shrine, but find an underground cell of Nemeth Gnostics guarding the waters while an Argossean naval detachment attacks to seize the Fountain. The PCs must choose whether to strike a deal with the fanatical cultists, bribe the Argosseans, or secure the waters before the shrine collapses.</p>\n\n<div class=\"dc-box\">\n  <strong>Suggested Skill Checks:</strong> DC 15 Perception Check (spot Argossean mountain scouts); DC 17 Religion Check (quote Gnostic scripture accurately to secure sanctuary).\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"escalation\"><strong>Dynamic Escalation Trigger:</strong> On round 4 of combat inside the shrine, the fragile cavern ceiling collapses, destroying the primary pool of the Fountain forever and forcing a panicked flight.</p>\n",
